From: shuxueshuxue <98064968+shuxueshuxue@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:59:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] gugu: the adapter's own lookups use the config dir
 Claude Code reported

Why: claudeConfigDir() read the adapter's own CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, else
~/.claude. When a `claude` wrapper sets the variable inside the CLI's process,
the adapter does not see it, so its session index (session/list), live registry
(`<config>/sessions`), resume lookups (the resumed model and permission mode)
and subagent history all looked in the wrong directory. The transcript path the
CLI reports (previous patch) names the directory it really writes to:
claudeConfigDir() now returns that directory once a prompt has reported it,
ahead of the environment. Before the first report the adapter keeps the old
answer, and file watchers that are already running keep the root they started
with.

Upstream: none yet; goes with the previous patch.

Drop when: upstream learns the CLI's configuration directory from the CLI
itself, or the CLI exposes it to SDK clients.
